# Google OAuth client ID, shared by two independent optional features (each
# requests its own scope at runtime, so enabling one doesn't grant the
# other):
#   - read-only Google Calendar sync (ARCHITECTURE.md §7, "Google Calendar
#     integration")
#   - per-device Drive backup (ARCHITECTURE.md §7, "Drive backup") — also
#     needs the Google Drive API enabled in the same Cloud project
#     (APIs & Services -> Library -> Google Drive API -> Enable)
# Create one at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials as an
# "OAuth client ID" of type "Web application", with your dev origin (e.g.
# http://localhost:5173) and your deployed origin (e.g.
# https://<user>.github.io, or https://manifest.<subdomain>.workers.dev
# once on Cloudflare) added under "Authorized JavaScript origins".
# This ID is not secret — it's meant to be embedded in client-side apps —
# but it's specific to your Google Cloud project, so it isn't committed
# here.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored via *.local) for local dev, and
# set the same value as a repository variable named VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
# for the GitHub Pages build (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml).
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
